# #421 scoped execution decision

Decision: ALLOW scoped UI/test implementation and synthetic validation, under the human's explicit GitHub bug/deployment mandate. Source baseline c00bff678dfc9845c31742bc5d0d750fbbb9603e; original issue and four acceptance criteria saved before edits. Primary dirty checkout is excluded. C:/w-421 is the sole application writer; architecture agent read-only, NEW QA in a separate checkout after implementation. Serialized browser lane 7505 currently owned by root; no other writer or browser permitted concurrently.

Exact allowed application paths: ImportDocumentsWorkspace.tsx, ImportSession.css, new ImportEmptyStart.tsx, new __tests__/importEmpty.test.ts under frontend/src/components/shared/import. Test initially used .test.tsx, then moved to .test.ts with createElement so the existing full-suite discovery includes it; no runner/config change. No backend/API/schema/auth/provider/key/config/dependency changes. No actual clinical database writes, real documents, camera hardware or provider execution. Clinical network requests are intercepted with synthetic fixtures before wire; online requests only compiled static resources. Root owns integration; QA owns only evidence/test artifacts. Every attempt and pre-run snapshot retained.

Release is not granted by a Ruflo registration/lease/PID. A separate root release decision must bind a clean application commit, independent QA, root rerun, baseline-failure delta, privacy/scoped security, exact Vercel READY build, and pinned public screenshot hashes before closure. This record authorizes no unrelated capabilities, installs, worktree deletion, or global-green claim. Existing twelve frontend failures and one backend CI scope failure must be explicitly compared, not erased.
